{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761768, "segment_id": "6SQqSU7dOy", "segment_broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction John Seigenthaler (New York)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761768, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761768, "segment_id": "PlPsh7hrSP", "segment_broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "segment_title": "Campaign 2004 / Bush vs. Kerry / The Economy", "segment_description": "(Studio: John Seigenthaler)  Report introduced. \n (Kennebunkport, Maine: Norah O'Donnell)  President Bush's campaign response to the disappointing jobs numbers featured; scenes shown from Kennebunkport, Maine, where the president is attending a family wedding; details given of the economic challenges.  [In Michigan, BUSH&nbsp- says we \"turned the corner\" on jobs.]  \"Time\" magazine poll findings on the people's view of whom they trust to handle the economy cited.  [Political analyst Stuart ROTHENBERG&#134;- compares the approaches of the two Presidents Bush to the economy.] \n (Studio: John Seigenthaler)  Report introduced. \n (La Junta, Colorado: Carl Quintanilla)  Senator John Kerry's campaigning on the issue of the economy in the West featured; scenes shown from La Junta, Colorado & the campaign train.  [KERRY&nbsp- campaigns.]  [Two VOTERS&nbsp- offer views.]", "segment_duration": 280, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761769, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761768, "segment_id": "zND0DYOt5A", "segment_broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "segment_title": "Iraq / Fighting", "segment_description": "(Studio: John Seigenthaler)  Report introduced. \n (Baghdad: Jennifer Eccleston)  The battle by Marines against militias loyal to Shiite cleric Muqtada al-Sadr featured; scenes shown from the holy city of Najaf, where fighting has been going on since Thursday & from Baghdad's Sadr City.  [Marine Lt. Mike BORNEO&#134;- describes the intense fighting.]  [Iraqi interim Prime Minister Iyad ALLAWI&nbsp- says he has been getting positive message from al-Sadr.]  Allawi's signing of an amnesty law for insurgents noted. \n (Studio: John Seigenthaler)  The interim government's closing of the Arab TV network Al Jazeera for promoting violence noted.", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63330.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761770, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761768, "segment_id": "YVUi893WON", "segment_broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "segment_title": "Terrorism / Al Qaeda / Britain", "segment_description": "(Studio: John Seigenthaler)  The arrest in Dubai of Qari Akhtar&#134;&#134;, a radical Islamic leader who has been linked to Al Qaeda & to last year's plot to kill Pakistani President Pervez Musharraf, reported.   (London: Charles Sabine)  The busy week for British security services in combatting terrorism reviewed; details given of the arrests of Babar Ahmad&#134;&#134; & Muhammad Khan & other Al Qaeda suspects, including Eisa al-Hindi, author of \"The Army of Madinah in Kashmir,\" who is said to have led the Al Qaeda surveillance of landmarked buildings in the US & of the extent in London of the network of Islamic extremists.  [Terrorism expert M.J. GOHEL&#134;- says this may be the tip of the iceberg.]   (Studio: John Seigenthaler)  Further coverage of the war on terrorism on \"Meet the Press\" noted.", "segment_duration": 180, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63480.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761771, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761768, "segment_id": "314Jj9cf14", "segment_broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: John Seigenthaler)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 10, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63660.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761772, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761768, "segment_id": "ZNhD9Rm1Re", "segment_broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "segment_title": "(Commercial: Nexium; Pearle Vision; L.L. Bean; Ambien; Frosted Flakes/Fruit Loops.)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 3, "segment_start_time": "63670.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761773, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Commercial", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761768, "segment_id": "Nnms16yCPe", "segment_broadcast_id": "h9wwH1Kqk2", "segment_title": "In Depth (Olympic Games)", "segment_description": "(Studio: John Seigenthaler)  Report introduced. \n (Athens: Rehema Ellis)  The efforts by the International Olympic Committee on the eve of the Olympic Games in Athens, Greece, to deal with the problem of athletes & banned substances examined; details given about the case of US sprinter Torri Edwards, who tested positive for a banned stimulant.  [International Olympic Committee president Jacques ROGGE\u2020- states a zero tolerance policy.]  [\"Los Angeles Times\" sportswriter Alan ABRAHAMSON\u2020- talks about the cat & mouse game between the cheaters & the testers.]", "segm